      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Destination Handover, Odometer Sign-Off &amp; Joint Condition Inspection for Bike Transportation In Panchkula</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">When a two‑wheeler or motorcycle reaches its destination, a thorough handover process ensures that the vehicle’s condition, mileage, and documentation are accurately verified.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>This protects both the logistics provider and the customer, minimizing disputes and maintaining trust.</span></li><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>The handover is performed under daylight conditions to allow a clear visual inspection, and it follows three core checkpoints: condition re‑inspection, odometer verification, and signed condition sign‑off.</span></li></ul>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Daylight Condition Re‑inspection vs. Pickup Photos</strong>
    <ul>
      <li>Position the vehicle in a well‑lit area, preferably with natural sunlight, to reveal any scratches, dents, or cosmetic issues.</li>
      <li>Compare the live view with the original pickup photographs taken at the origin point. Use a side‑by‑side digital display or printed copies.</li>
      <li>Mark any discrepancies—new scratches, paint chips, or missing accessories—on a dedicated inspection sheet.</li>
      <li>Take fresh photographs of the vehicle from the same angles as the pickup images to document its final state.</li>
      <li>Confirm that all original accessories (helmets, locks, spare parts) are present and undamaged.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>

  <li><strong>Odometer Verification against the LR Bilty</strong>
    <ul>
      <li>Read the current odometer reading directly from the instrument cluster, ensuring the display is clear and unobstructed.</li>
      <li>Cross‑check this reading with the mileage recorded on the Logistics Receipt (LR) bilty that accompanied the shipment.</li>
      <li>If the reading exceeds the LR mileage, note the variance and investigate possible causes (e.g., test rides, unauthorized use).</li>
      <li>Document the verified odometer value on the handover form, and have the driver or carrier sign to acknowledge the reading.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>

  <li><strong>Signed Condition Sign‑off</strong>
    <ul>
      <li>Present the completed inspection sheet, the new photographs, and the odometer verification to the recipient.</li>
      <li>Both the receiver and the delivery representative sign the form, confirming agreement on the vehicle’s condition and mileage.</li>
      <li>Provide the recipient with a copy of the signed document and the photo set for their records.</li>
      <li>Retain the original signed form in the shipment file for future reference and dispute resolution.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
</ul>

<p>By following these steps under daylight conditions, the handover process ensures transparency, reduces the risk of post‑delivery claims, and guarantees that the two‑wheeler or motorcycle reaches its new owner exactly as expected.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>



